Root cause:
The bug was caused by a potential overflow when calculating new memory map (mmap) page entries within a 32-bit limit. The existing implementation did not check if the addition of the current mmap pages to the new length (converted to pages) would exceed the maximum representable value in a 32-bit integer, which could lead to memory corruption or crashes. This was addressed by adding an overflow check before performing the addition.
